## 1. My Testing Approach

The application is a Task Management Application where a user can register, log in and manage tasks. Since the application is close to production and there is no existing test documentation, I would first understand the complete user flow and then test each feature individually as well as together.

I would mainly focus on:

* Whether the user can register and log in correctly.
* Whether invalid information is properly rejected.
* Whether a logged-in user can create, view, edit and delete tasks.
* Whether the task data is actually saved correctly in the database.
* Whether one user can access another user's tasks.
* Whether the application gives proper error messages when something goes wrong.
* Boundary cases such as empty values, very long inputs and special characters.

I would start with the basic positive cases and then move towards negative and edge cases. For a production-ready application, I would give more importance to authentication, authorization and database-related issues because these can affect user data.

