# 4. Task Creation

Once the login functionality is working, I would test the task creation feature.

### Test Case 1 – Create a Valid Task

I would log in, enter valid task information and click Save/Create.

**Expected result:**
The task should be created successfully and should appear in the task list.

### Test Case 2 – Create Task Without Required Information

I would leave the required task field empty and click Save.

**Expected result:**
The task should not be created and the user should see a validation message.

### Test Case 3 – Only Spaces

I would enter spaces instead of actual task information.

**Expected result:**
The application should reject the input rather than creating an empty-looking task.

### Test Case 4 – Very Long Task

I would enter a very large amount of text.

**Expected result:**
The application should either restrict the input or display a proper validation message. It should not crash.

### Test Case 5 – Special Characters

I would create a task containing normal special characters.

**Expected result:**
The task should be saved and displayed correctly.

### Test Case 6 – Multiple Tasks

I would create several tasks one after another.

**Expected result:**
All tasks should appear separately. Creating a new task should not overwrite an existing task.

### Test Case 7 – Database Persistence

After creating a task, I would refresh the page and also log out and log in again.

**Expected result:**
The task should still be available because tasks are stored in the database.

