# 9. Important Edge Cases

Apart from normal testing, I would check some less common situations because these can expose bugs that normal testing may miss.

### 1. Double-clicking Save

If the user clicks the Save button twice quickly, the application should ideally create only one task.

### 2. Refresh During an Operation

I would check what happens if the user refreshes the page after creating or editing a task.

### 3. Very Long Input

Large input should not break the UI or cause a database error.

### 4. Whitespace

Inputs containing only spaces should not be accepted as valid information.

### 5. Multiple Users

I would use separate accounts and verify that their task data remains separate.

### 6. Empty Task List

A newly registered user may not have any tasks. The application should handle this situation properly.

### 7. Session Expiry

If the session expires, the application should ask the user to log in again rather than showing an unexpected error.

